## GitHub’s official MCP Server

If you mean **GitHub Copilot CLI**, you do **not** need to install or configure GitHub’s MCP server: it is built in already. Verify its status with:

```bash
copilot mcp list
copilot mcp get github
```

GitHub Copilot CLI’s user-added MCP configuration lives at `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json`; use `copilot mcp add` only for *other* MCP servers. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli/customize-copilot/add-mcp-servers))

## For VS Code / Claude / Cursor / another MCP host

The simplest official setup is GitHub’s hosted remote MCP endpoint:

```json
{
  "servers": {
    "github": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/"
    }
  }
}
```

Use an MCP host that supports remote MCP and OAuth; GitHub lists VS Code 1.101+ among supported clients. ([github.com](https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server?locale=en-US))

## Local Docker configuration

Use this if your host needs a local stdio MCP server. Set a fine-scoped PAT first:

```bash
export GITHUB_PAT=your_token_here
```

Then configure:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "servers": {
      "github": {
        "command": "docker",
        "args": [
          "run",
          "-i",
          "--rm",
          "-e",
          "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN",
          "ghcr.io/github/github-mcp-server"
        ],
        "env": {
          "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "$GITHUB_PAT"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

GitHub recommends keeping tokens in environment variables rather than committing them in configuration files. ([github.com](https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server?locale=en-US))

## Limit exposed capabilities

For a safer/minimal setup, add toolsets:

```json
"env": {
  "GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN": "$GITHUB_PAT",
  "GITHUB_TOOLSETS": "repos,issues,pull_requests"
}
```

Or run read-only mode with `GITHUB_READ_ONLY=1`. By default, the server includes `context`, `repos`, `issues`, `pull_requests`, and `users`. ([github.com](https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server?locale=en-US))

